<usx version="3.1">
<book code="2JN" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">2 John</para>

<para style="toc1">2 John</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2JN 1"/>

<para style="s">A Greeting from the Elder</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="2JN 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">3 John 1:1–4</char></note>The elder, To the chosen lady and her children, whom I love in truth, and not only I, but also all those having known the truth— <verse eid="2JN 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2JN 1:2"/>because of the truth remaining in us and <char style="add">that</char> will be with us to the age: <verse eid="2JN 1:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2JN 1:3"/>Grace, mercy, <char style="add">and</char> peace will be with us from God the Father and from Jesus Christ,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and from the Lord Jesus Christ</char></note> the Son of the Father, in truth and love. <verse eid="2JN 1:3"/></para>

<para style="s">Walking in the TruthJohn 8:30–47</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2JN 1:4"/>I rejoiced exceedingly that I have found some of your children walking in truth, just as we received a commandment from the Father. <verse eid="2JN 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2JN 1:5"/>And now I implore you, lady, not as writing to you a new commandment, but that which we have had from the beginning, that we should love one another. <verse eid="2JN 1:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2JN 1:6"/>And this is love, that we should walk according to His commandments. This is the commandment, just as you⁺ heard from the beginning, so that you⁺ should walk in it. <verse eid="2JN 1:6"/></para>

<para style="s">Beware of Deceivers</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2JN 1:7"/>For many deceivers went out<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">entered</char></note> into the world, those not confessing Jesus Christ coming in flesh. This is the deceiver and the antichrist. <verse eid="2JN 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2JN 1:8"/>Watch yourselves, so that you⁺ may not lose what things we worked for,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TH, NE, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">what you have worked for</char></note> but you⁺ may receive a full reward. <verse eid="2JN 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2JN 1:9"/>Everyone going on ahead<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Everyone transgressing</char></note> and not remaining in the teaching of Christ does not have God. The one remaining in the teaching,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the teaching of Christ</char></note> this one has both the Father and the Son. <verse eid="2JN 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2JN 1:10"/>If anyone comes to you⁺ and does not bring this teaching, do not receive him into the house, and do not speak to him to greet <char style="add">him</char>. <verse eid="2JN 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2JN 1:11"/>For the one speaking to him to greet <char style="add">him</char> partakes in his evil works. <verse eid="2JN 1:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Conclusion3 John 1:13–14</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2JN 1:12"/>Having many things to write to you⁺, I intended not with paper and ink, but I hope to come to you⁺ and to speak mouth to mouth,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">face to face</char></note> so that our<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">your</char></note> joy may be full. <verse eid="2JN 1:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2JN 1:13"/>The children of your chosen sister greet you.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Amen.</char></note> <verse eid="2JN 1:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="2JN 1"/>

</usx>
